💼 Employee Salary Calculation using C++

📌 Description

This C++ program demonstrates Abstraction, Inheritance, and Polymorphism by calculating salaries for different types of employees.

The program supports:

- Permanent Employee
- Contract Employee

🧠 Concepts Used

- Abstract Class
- Pure Virtual Function
- Inheritance
- Polymorphism
- Function Overriding
- Encapsulation
- Constructors

⚙️ Working

- "Employee" is an abstract base class.
- It stores the employee ID and name.
- "calculateSalary()" is declared as a pure virtual function.
- "PermanentEmployee" calculates salary using Basic Salary + Allowance.
- "ContractEmployee" calculates salary using Hourly Rate × Hours Worked.
- "displayPaySlip()" uses a base-class reference to display employee details and salary for both employee types.

💰 Salary Calculation

Permanent Employee

Salary = Basic Salary + Allowance

Contract Employee

Salary = Hourly Rate × Hours Worked

